Package: grub-btrfs
Version: 4.14-2
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Shadowfetch Project <signing@shadowfetch.com>
Installed-Size: 99
Depends: btrfs-progs, inotify-tools
Recommends: grub-common | grub2-common, snapper
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/Antynea/grub-btrfs
Description: Include Btrfs snapshots as GRUB boot entries (vendored v4.14)
 grub-btrfs adds a GRUB submenu listing your Btrfs snapshots so a broken
 upgrade is one reboot away from a known-good system. The grub-btrfsd daemon
 watches the snapshot directory and regenerates the menu automatically.
 .
 Vendored from upstream Antynea/grub-btrfs v4.14 (GPL-3+) by Shadowfetch Linux
 because the Debian package is not currently available in testing.
